#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The examples in this section illustrate some common ways to use the Executor"
" primitive. Before running these examples, follow the instructions in "
"[Install Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) and [Executor "
"quickstart](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"
msgstr ""
"Los ejemplos en esta sección ilustran algunas formas comunes de usar la "
"primitiva Executor. Antes de ejecutar estos ejemplos, sigue las "
"instrucciones en [Instalar Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) y [Inicio rápido "
"con Executor](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin {#before-you-begin}"
msgstr "Antes de comenzar {#before-you-begin}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some of the code examples on this page use `samplex`, which is part of the "
"Samplomatic package.  Therefore, before running those code block, you must "
"install Samplomatic, as shown in the following code block.  For more "
"information, see the [Samplomatic "
"documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic).\n"
msgstr ""
"Algunos de los ejemplos de código en esta página usan `samplex`, que es "
"parte del paquete Samplomatic. Por lo tanto, antes de ejecutar esos bloques "
"de código, debes instalar Samplomatic, como se muestra en el siguiente "
"bloque de código. Para más información, consulta la [documentación de "
"Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Parameterized circuit {#example-parameterized-circuit}"
msgstr "Ejemplo: Circuito parametrizado {#example-parameterized-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example illustrates how to add circuit items with parameters, as well as how to add samplex items. It consists of these steps:\n"
"1. Set up the circuit: Generate and transpile the target circuit.\n"
"2. Prepare a samplex: Group gates and measurements into annotated boxes and generate the circuit template and samplex pair.\n"
"3. Execute: Add a circuit item and a samplex item to a `QuantumProgram` and execute both in a single job.\n"
msgstr ""
"Este ejemplo ilustra cómo agregar elementos de circuito con parámetros, así como cómo agregar elementos samplex. Consiste en estos pasos:\n"
"1. Configurar el circuito: Generar y transpilar el circuito objetivo.\n"
"2. Preparar un samplex: Agrupar los gates y las mediciones en cajas anotadas y generar el par de circuito template y samplex.\n"
"3. Ejecutar: Agregar un elemento de circuito y un elemento samplex a un `QuantumProgram` y ejecutar ambos en un único job.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the circuit {#set-up-the-circuit}"
msgstr "Configurar el circuito {#set-up-the-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prepare a three-qubit GHZ state, rotate the qubits around the Pauli-Z axis, "
"and measures the qubits in the computational basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Preparar un estado GHZ de tres qubits, rotar los qubits alrededor del eje de"
" Pauli-Z, y medir los qubits en la base computacional.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specify the backend and transpile the circuit to only use instructions "
"supported by the QPU (referred to as an instruction set architecture (ISA) "
"circuit).\n"
msgstr ""
"Especificar el backend y transpilar el circuito para usar únicamente las "
"instrucciones admitidas por el QPU (denominado circuito de arquitectura de "
"conjunto de instrucciones (ISA)).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the samplex {#prepare-the-samplex}"
msgstr "Preparar el samplex {#prepare-the-samplex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `generate_boxing_pass_manager` convenience function and its twirling"
" parameters to group two-qubit gates and measurements into boxes and apply "
"twirling annotations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usar la función de conveniencia `generate_boxing_pass_manager` y sus "
"parámetros de twirling para agrupar los gates de dos qubits y las mediciones"
" en cajas y aplicar anotaciones de twirling.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `build` method to generate the template circuit and the samplex.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usar el método `build` para generar el circuito template y el samplex.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the circuits {#execute-the-circuits}"
msgstr "Ejecutar los circuitos {#execute-the-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Executor runs `QuantumProgram` objects. Each `QuantumProgram` can contain "
"several items. This example adds a circuit item and a samplex item for "
"execution. For full details, see [Executor input and "
"output](/guides/executor-input-output).\n"
msgstr ""
"Executor ejecuta objetos `QuantumProgram`. Cada `QuantumProgram` puede "
"contener varios elementos. Este ejemplo agrega un elemento de circuito y un "
"elemento samplex para la ejecución. Para obtener todos los detalles, "
"consulta [Entrada y salida del Executor](/guides/executor-input-output).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first step is to initialize an empty program, requesting `1024` shots "
"for each configuration of each item.\n"
msgstr ""
"El primer paso es inicializar un programa vacío, solicitando `1024` shots "
"para cada configuración de cada elemento.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Append the circuit item to the `QuantumProgram`. This circuit item consists "
"of two parts - the ISA circuit and 10 sets of its parameter values.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agregar el elemento de circuito al `QuantumProgram`. Este elemento de "
"circuito consta de dos partes: el circuito ISA y 10 conjuntos de sus valores"
" de parámetros.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Append the samplex item to the `QuantumProgram` with these arguments:\n"
"- The template circuit and the samplex generated by the `build` function\n"
"- Ten sets of parameter values for the original circuit\n"
"- The number of randomizations to perform\n"
msgstr ""
"Agregar el elemento samplex al `QuantumProgram` con estos argumentos:\n"
"- El circuito template y el samplex generados por la función `build`\n"
"- Diez conjuntos de valores de parámetros para el circuito original\n"
"- El número de randomizaciones a realizar\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the Executor job {#run-the-executor-job}"
msgstr "Ejecutar el job de Executor {#run-the-executor-job}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve the result for each task.\n"
msgstr "Recuperar el resultado para cada tarea.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Perform PEC {#example-perform-pec}"
msgstr "Ejemplo: Realizar PEC {#example-perform-pec}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example shows how to use a samplex item to perform probabilistic error "
"cancellation ([PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-"
"techniques#pec)) for error mitigation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Este ejemplo muestra cómo usar un elemento samplex para realizar la "
"cancelación de errores probabilista ([PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-"
"suppression-techniques#pec)) para la mitigación de errores.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider a mirrored-version of a circuit with ten qubits and two unique layers of CX gates. These are the main tasks:\n"
"- Execute the circuit with twirling.\n"
"- Execute the circuit with PEC mitigation, as in the paper [\"Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy quantum processors\"](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866).\n"
msgstr ""
"Considera una versión espejo de un circuito con diez qubits y dos capas únicas de gates CX. Estas son las tareas principales:\n"
"- Ejecutar el circuito con twirling.\n"
"- Ejecutar el circuito con mitigación PEC, como en el artículo [\"Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy quantum processors\"](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pipeline consists of these steps:\n"
"1. Set up: Generate the target circuit and group its operations into boxes.\n"
"2. Learn: Learn the noise of the instructions that we want to mitigate with PEC.\n"
"3. Execute: Run the circuit on a backend.\n"
"4. Analyze: Post-process and analyze the results.\n"
msgstr ""
"El pipeline consiste en estos pasos:\n"
"1. Configuración: Generar el circuito objetivo y agrupar sus operaciones en cajas.\n"
"2. Aprendizaje: Aprender el ruido de las instrucciones que queremos mitigar con PEC.\n"
"3. Ejecución: Ejecutar el circuito en un backend.\n"
"4. Análisis: Post-procesar y analizar los resultados.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For comparison, we will run this mirrored circuit twice. Once with only "
"Pauli-twirling applied, and once withe PEC mitigation applied.\n"
msgstr ""
"A modo de comparación, ejecutaremos este circuito espejo dos veces. Una vez "
"con solo Pauli-twirling aplicado, y otra vez con la mitigación PEC "
"aplicada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The usage for this example is approximately 10 minutes on a Heron r2 processor.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"El uso para este ejemplo es de aproximadamente 10 minutos en un procesador Heron r2.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the circuit {#set-up-the-circuit-1}"
msgstr "Configurar el circuito {#set-up-the-circuit-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a backend and prepare a 10-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Elegir un backend y preparar un circuito de 10 qubits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f9e93b2c-154a-4d09-872d-f770bcc669c4-0.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f9e93b2c-154a-4d09-872d-f770bcc669c4-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Combine the circuit with its inverse to create a mirror circuit.\n"
msgstr "Combinar el circuito con su inverso para crear un circuito espejo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f8ac3f75-88ca-40f9-8382-6a427303bb8e-0.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f8ac3f75-88ca-40f9-8382-6a427303bb8e-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set some parameter values:\n"
msgstr "Establecer algunos valores de parámetros:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the pass manager to transpile the circuit to become an ISA circuit.\n"
msgstr "Usar el pass manager para transpilar el circuito a un circuito ISA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, group gates and measurements into annotated boxes. You can do this "
"manually or use the `generate_boxing_pass_manager` function from Samplomatic"
" for convenience. The first circuit will only have twirling applied and "
"therefore only needs the `Twirl` annotation. The second circuit will be run "
"with full PEC mitigation and needs both `Twirl` and `InjectNoise` "
"annotations.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, agrupar los gates y las mediciones en cajas anotadas. Puedes"
" hacerlo manualmente o usar la función `generate_boxing_pass_manager` de "
"Samplomatic para mayor comodidad. El primer circuito solo tendrá twirling "
"aplicado y por lo tanto solo necesita la anotación `Twirl`. El segundo "
"circuito se ejecutará con mitigación PEC completa y necesita las anotaciones"
" `Twirl` e `InjectNoise`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise {#learn-the-noise}"
msgstr "Aprender el ruido {#learn-the-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To minimize the number of noise learning experiments, identify the unique instructions in the second circuit (the one with boxes annotated with `InjectNoise`). In defining uniqueness, two box instructions are equal if both of the following are true:\n"
"- Their content is equal, up to single-qubit gates.\n"
"- Their `Twirl` annotation is equal (every other annotation is disregarded).\n"
msgstr ""
"Para minimizar el número de experimentos de aprendizaje del ruido, identificar las instrucciones únicas en el segundo circuito (el que tiene cajas anotadas con `InjectNoise`). Para definir la unicidad, dos instrucciones de caja son iguales si ambas de las siguientes son verdaderas:\n"
"- Su contenido es igual, salvo por los gates de un solo qubit.\n"
"- Su anotación `Twirl` es igual (cualquier otra anotación se ignora).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This leads to three unique instructions, namely the odd and even gate boxes,"
" and the final measurement box.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto lleva a tres instrucciones únicas, a saber las cajas de gates pares e "
"impares, y la caja de medición final.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Initialize a `NoiseLearnerV3`, choose the learning parameters by setting its"
" options, and run a noise learning job.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inicializar un `NoiseLearnerV3`, elegir los parámetros de aprendizaje "
"configurando sus opciones, y ejecutar un job de aprendizaje del ruido.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Convert `result` to the object required by the samplex by using the "
"`result.to_dict` method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Convertir `result` al objeto requerido por el samplex usando el método "
"`result.to_dict`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the circuits {#execute-the-circuits-1}"
msgstr "Ejecutar los circuitos {#execute-the-circuits-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Executor` runs `QuantumProgram` objects. Each `QuantumProgram` can contain "
"several *items*, which are appended to the program. Each item is a task for "
"the program to perform.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Executor` ejecuta objetos `QuantumProgram`. Cada `QuantumProgram` puede "
"contener varios *elementos*, que se añaden al programa. Cada elemento es una"
" tarea que el programa debe realizar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Initialize an empty program, requesting `1000` shots for each configuration "
"of each item.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inicializar un programa vacío, solicitando `1000` shots para cada "
"configuración de cada elemento.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, build the template circuit and samplex for `mirror_circuit_twirl` and "
"append them to the program. Also request `900` randomizations from the "
"samplex. This means that the samplex will generate `900` sets of parameters,"
" and each set will be executed `1000` times (the number of shots) in the "
"QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, construir el circuito template y el samplex para "
"`mirror_circuit_twirl` y añadirlos al programa. También solicitar `900` "
"randomizaciones al samplex. Esto significa que el samplex generará `900` "
"conjuntos de parámetros, y cada conjunto se ejecutará `1000` veces (el "
"número de shots) en el QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is the program's first task (result 0).\n"
msgstr "Esta es la primera tarea del programa (resultado 0).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, append the template circuit and samplex built for "
"`mirror_circuit_pec`, requesting `900` randomizations.  This is the "
"program's second task (result 1).\n"
msgstr ""
"Del mismo modo, añadir el circuito template y el samplex construidos para "
"`mirror_circuit_pec`, solicitando `900` randomizaciones. Esta es la segunda "
"tarea del programa (resultado 1).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import `Executor` and submit a job.\n"
msgstr "Importar `Executor` y enviar un job.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze results {#analyze-results}"
msgstr "Analizar los resultados {#analyze-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, post-process the results to estimate the expectation values of "
"single-qubit Pauli-Z operators acting on each of the ten active qubits "
"(expected value: `1.0`).\n"
msgstr ""
"Por último, post-procesar los resultados para estimar los valores esperados "
"de los operadores de Pauli-Z de un solo qubit actuando sobre cada uno de los"
" diez qubits activos (valor esperado: `1.0`).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Próximos pasos {#next-steps}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- Review the [broadcasting](/guides/primitive-input-output#broadcasting) overview.\n"
"- Learn how to use [Executor options](/guides/executor-options).\n"
"- Understand the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"
"- Review the [Samplomatic documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/).\n"
"- Learn about how to combine different error mitigation techniques when using directed execution model in the [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html) tutorial.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recomendaciones\">\n"
"- Revisa el resumen de [broadcasting](/guides/primitive-input-output#broadcasting).\n"
"- Aprende a usar las [opciones del Executor](/guides/executor-options).\n"
"- Comprende el [modelo de ejecución dirigida](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"
"- Consulta la [documentación de Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/).\n"
"- Aprende a combinar diferentes técnicas de mitigación de errores al usar el modelo de ejecución dirigida en el tutorial [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
